        <pluginType>Topic</pluginType>
        <scope>Visit Activity Logger is responsible for capturing, updating, and validating on‑ground visit execution data for retail locations within the VyuhX platform.
Its scope is to ensure that field visits conducted using Consumer Goods Cloud Visit Execution are accurately logged, enriched with observations, and reflected back into Salesforce so that AI‑driven expansion, demand, and readiness decisions remain grounded in real‑world execution.
This sub‑agent acts as the human‑in‑the‑loop execution bridge, closing the gap between Data Cloud analytics and on‑site reality.
 
In Scope (What It Does)
Log activities performed during a site visit
Update visit status and outcomes
Capture field observations (footfall, competition, visibility, issues)
Track task completion during visits
Calculate and assign a Visit Execution Score
Adjust confidence for AI recommendations
Feed visit outcomes back into retail readiness and expansion logic

Out of Scope (What It Does NOT Do)
Does not create visits (handled by Visit Creation Assistant)
Does not calculate demand, financial, or competition scores directly
Does not override AI recommendations autonomously
Does not manage routing, scheduling, or workforce planning</scope>
